The modern AMIX cross compiler: gcc 14.2.0 with C and C++ (libstdc++,
exceptions, RTTI) and binutils 2.43.1 for m68k-elf, the ABI of AMIX 2.1
userland on the Amiga, in /opt/m68k-amix.  Its specs link AMIX programs
against the AMIX sysroot (/opt/m68k-amix-sysroot), and libamixc99 adds the
C99 and POSIX functions AMIX's libc predates.  Code built with -mcpu=68060
has no 64-bit multiply or divide, so it runs on every 68020-68060.

For applications; the kernel and drivers use amix-gcc-27.
